00:16:09,943 --> 00:16:11,423
I changed my mind, Shiori.

206
00:16:11,423 --> 00:16:13,823
I want you to do three. Yeah, three.

207
00:16:13,823 --> 00:16:15,573
Three? All right.

208
00:16:15,573 --> 00:16:18,203
Just for you, but you have to be specific.

209
00:16:18,203 --> 00:16:19,523
What do you want me to do?

210
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:21,873
Hmm, for the first one,

211
00:16:21,873 --> 00:16:23,733
maybe you could unleash

212
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:26,573
your patented Shiori beam.

213
00:16:26,573 --> 00:16:27,453
My Shiori beam?

214
00:16:27,793 --> 00:16:30,973
Ah, fine, just for you.

215
00:16:30,973 --> 00:16:32,773
Okay.

216
00:16:32,773 --> 00:16:37,503
The... Shiori...

217
00:16:38,243 --> 00:16:39,223
Beam!

218
00:16:39,223 --> 00:16:43,943
Oh. Oh, um, uh, ah.

219
00:16:43,943 --> 00:16:45,053
That was—that was pretty close.

220
00:16:45,053 --> 00:16:46,763
I can, can you do it again?
Can you do it again?

221
00:16:46,763 --> 00:16:47,883
Uh, maybe this time,

222
00:16:47,883 --> 00:16:49,233
shout something like cool,
shout something cool,

223
00:16:49,233 --> 00:16:51,513
like, 'Explosion!'

224
00:16:51,513 --> 00:16:53,723
I think you're expecting too much from me.

225
00:16:53,723 --> 00:16:54,703
How about we do something else?

226
00:16:55,363 --> 00:16:56,913
Uh, okay, fine.
Ugh, okay, fine.

227
00:16:56,913 --> 00:16:59,913
Hmm. Oh, I know,

228
00:16:59,913 --> 00:17:01,103
for the next one,

229
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,273
you have a lot of people watching, right?

230
00:17:03,653 --> 00:17:06,693
I want you to rizz up the audience.

231
00:17:06,693 --> 00:17:07,163
Yeah.

232
00:17:07,163 --> 00:17:10,623
Can you like, cavort on the camera?

233
00:17:10,623 --> 00:17:12,753
And then, and then give us your best line.

234
00:17:12,753 --> 00:17:13,653
Yeah, do that.

235
00:17:13,653 --> 00:17:15,623
Is this like your secret fantasy, bebs?

236
00:17:16,063 --> 00:17:17,463
Uhh, no, just—just do it.

237
00:17:17,463 --> 00:17:19,503
Just do it. I'm in charge here, okay?

238
00:17:19,503 --> 00:17:22,043
Ah, that's what you want, huh?

239
00:17:22,783 --> 00:17:24,523
But tonight,

240
00:17:24,523 --> 00:17:25,363
I'm using you.

241
00:17:25,363 --> 00:17:26,583
Shiori!

242
00:17:26,583 --> 00:17:27,113
Why?

243
00:17:27,113 --> 00:17:28,973
What?

244
00:17:28,973 --> 00:17:29,653
Ah.

245
00:17:29,653 --> 00:17:30,963
Are you okay there, my girl?

246
00:17:32,503 --> 00:17:34,813
Yeah, yeah. All good.

247
00:17:34,813 --> 00:17:38,283
You guys are supposed to be rizzing the rizzah.

248
00:17:38,283 --> 00:17:39,843
You're supposed to be rizzing everybody else.

249
00:17:39,843 --> 00:17:42,883
But she's always rizz'd, though.

250
00:17:42,883 --> 00:17:44,923
I'm—I'm sure everybody

251
00:17:44,923 --> 00:17:45,953
is blushing now, right?

252
00:17:45,953 --> 00:17:46,503
That sounds pretty good.

253
00:17:46,783 --> 00:17:47,813
I don't know.

254
00:17:47,813 --> 00:17:49,283
Oh well, okay,

255
00:17:49,283 --> 00:17:50,913
I have a third one for you.

256
00:17:50,913 --> 00:17:52,013
Are you ready?

257
00:17:52,363 --> 00:17:54,053
Sure, just for you.

258
00:17:54,053 --> 00:17:57,093
Okay, for this last one,

259
00:17:57,093 --> 00:17:58,583
I want you to pretend

260
00:17:58,583 --> 00:17:59,913
that the darkness is consuming you

261
00:17:59,913 --> 00:18:00,703
and you're in danger,

262
00:18:00,703 --> 00:18:03,523
and the only thing that will save your life

263
00:18:03,523 --> 00:18:05,183
is if you hit the biggest dab ever.

264
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:08,593
Uhh, the things I do for love.

265
00:18:08,593 --> 00:18:11,923
Okay. How's this?

266
00:18:11,923 --> 00:18:13,283
Dab!

267
00:18:13,283 --> 00:18:14,253
Shiori!

268
00:18:14,253 --> 00:18:15,593
Wow, that was weak.

269
00:18:15,593 --> 00:18:17,543
That's not fighting for your life.

270
00:18:17,543 --> 00:18:19,453
That's like you're bored.

271
00:18:19,453 --> 00:18:21,043
Okay, do it again.

272
00:18:21,043 --> 00:18:22,593
But this time, power, energy,

273
00:18:22,593 --> 00:18:23,983
powerful dab.

274
00:18:23,983 --> 00:18:25,133
Yes.

275
00:18:25,463 --> 00:18:28,943
Okay. Gotta get on my trauma here.

276
00:18:28,943 --> 00:18:32,013
Okay. Dab!

277
00:18:32,013 --> 00:18:34,603
Ooh! Okay, Shiori,

278
00:18:34,603 --> 00:18:36,663
that was pretty good.

279
00:18:36,663 --> 00:18:39,023
Now, can you like dab back and forth

280
00:18:39,023 --> 00:18:40,263
like 10 times over and over

281
00:18:40,263 --> 00:18:40,883
and over again?

282
00:18:40,883 --> 00:18:42,573
Okay, I think that's expecting

283
00:18:42,573 --> 00:18:43,283
too much, though.

284
00:18:43,283 --> 00:18:44,723
I think that's enough memes

285
00:18:44,723 --> 00:18:45,024
for you, bebs.

286
00:18:54,703 --> 00:18:56,273
Through her efforts,

287
00:18:56,273 --> 00:18:58,233
Shiori gained two apples

288
00:18:58,233 --> 00:19:00,353
that contain magical powers

289
00:19:00,353 --> 00:19:02,333
from all of her cringe.

290
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:04,453
Oh, I can make the apples kiss.

291
00:19:05,153 --> 00:19:07,063
All right, now that I have these sketchy items,

292
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,603
I'm a head out of here.

293
00:19:18,503 --> 00:19:20,013
All right.

294
00:19:20,013 --> 00:19:22,983
Where do I put these apples?

295
00:19:22,983 --> 00:19:25,623
That's not how it works, Shiori.

296
00:19:25,623 --> 00:19:26,723
You're trying to jump ahead,

297
00:19:26,723 --> 00:19:28,193
but you got to do the trials in order.

298
00:19:28,493 --> 00:19:30,853
Uhh, all right.

299
00:19:30,853 --> 00:19:32,513
What do?

300
00:19:32,513 --> 00:19:33,483
You need to do all the dabs, okay?

301
00:19:35,373 --> 00:19:36,933
Come on. I'll help you

302
00:19:36,933 --> 00:19:38,233
unlock the pink book. Got it.

303
00:19:39,173 --> 00:19:40,883
Oh, fine, fine. The Nyakuzas want to help.

304
00:19:41,903 --> 00:19:45,423
All right, pink book, let's see.

305
00:19:45,423 --> 00:19:48,913
This one.

306
00:19:48,913 --> 00:19:50,043
Nyakuza?

307
00:19:50,043 --> 00:19:53,103
Uh, they say that that's the book of playtime.

308
00:19:53,103 --> 00:19:54,024
That's my favorite.

309
00:19:54,703 --> 00:19:58,293
All I have to do is juggle the apple.

310
00:19:58,293 --> 00:19:59,363
If you say so.

311
00:20:07,167 --> 00:20:11,787
You know, uh, juggling hasn't worked for me in the past.

312
00:20:13,947 --> 00:20:15,937
Oh, um, let me check what the script says, then.

313
00:20:16,177 --> 00:20:17,417
You have a script?

314
00:20:21,047 --> 00:20:22,407
Well, then do this.

315
00:20:23,047 --> 00:20:25,532
Please, everyone is having fun, so uh,

316
00:20:25,532 --> 00:20:28,217
even if you don't do it right, it's still good enough.

317
00:20:29,107 --> 00:20:29,447
Huh?

318
00:20:29,867 --> 00:20:31,817
Woah, if you're okay with good enough...

319
00:20:32,437 --> 00:20:33,487
...it's good enough for me.

320
00:20:34,057 --> 00:20:35,337
All right. Do your best.

321
00:20:35,717 --> 00:20:36,467
I'll try.

322
00:20:37,847 --> 00:20:38,777
All right, let's go.

323
00:20:38,777 --> 00:20:39,147
Oh.

324
00:20:39,327 --> 00:20:39,787
Ah.

325
00:20:39,847 --> 00:20:40,487
Oh.

326
00:20:41,257 --> 00:20:42,007
Ah, it's not too bad.

327
00:20:42,627 --> 00:20:43,117
Oh.

328
00:20:43,187 --> 00:20:43,867
Oh.

329
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:44,237
Ah.

330
00:20:44,237 --> 00:20:44,627
Oh.

331
00:20:44,637 --> 00:20:45,747
Spinning and juggling.

332
00:20:45,957 --> 00:20:46,397
Yeah.

333
00:20:46,467 --> 00:20:49,067
You like that? You're getting entertained, aren't you?

334
00:20:49,227 --> 00:20:49,827
Do your best.

335
00:20:50,007 --> 00:20:50,597
Yeah.

336
00:20:51,077 --> 00:20:52,927
Are you sure you weren't born to do this?

337
00:20:52,957 --> 00:20:55,807
Oh, you think you was born to be a clown?

338
00:20:57,207 --> 00:20:58,367
Nothing, you're a clown. You're Shiori.

339
00:20:58,657 --> 00:21:02,167
Oh, so have fun enough for you now, huh?

340
00:21:05,187 --> 00:21:07,447
How many once when you do this work?

341
00:21:07,757 --> 00:21:08,607
It's good enough, huh?

342
00:21:08,857 --> 00:21:09,967
Oh, my luck ran out.

343
00:21:13,377 --> 00:21:14,277
Oh, all right.

344
00:21:15,007 --> 00:21:16,177
Let's see what we got.

345
00:21:16,747 --> 00:21:17,687
Huh?

346
00:21:21,937 --> 00:21:23,077
Huh?

347
00:21:25,137 --> 00:21:28,207
It looks like you're getting a pot, huh? 'Cause uh...

348
00:21:28,207 --> 00:21:32,437
If there's an RPG section on the trials, then maybe you can use that pot as your helm.

349
00:21:33,437 --> 00:21:35,377
It does come with a plus three to magic.

350
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:35,877
Huh?

351
00:21:36,227 --> 00:21:36,597
Oh.

352
00:21:36,997 --> 00:21:37,727
Where does it say that, Bejoux?
Where does it say that, Bijou?

353
00:21:37,947 --> 00:21:39,147
Shiori.

354
00:21:42,237 --> 00:21:43,797
Is Shiori definitely equipped it then, huh?

355
00:21:43,867 --> 00:21:45,377
He just want me to look stupid.

356
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:48,367
Not like that, you know.

357
00:21:48,547 --> 00:21:52,447
This way you'll be ready just in case there's a boss fight.

358
00:21:52,657 --> 00:21:54,047
Fine.

359
00:21:55,737 --> 00:21:58,047
I'm only doing this because of love.

360
00:21:59,077 --> 00:21:59,637
Like this?

361
00:22:01,107 --> 00:22:07,277
Shiori, uh, apparently puts the cauldron on her head, it grants her the power of...

362
00:22:08,137 --> 00:22:09,947
I don't know, mild neck pain, probably.

363
00:22:10,187 --> 00:22:11,787
Shiori, is wearing that helping?

364
00:22:12,387 --> 00:22:14,367
No, but I feel kind of funny.

365
00:22:15,577 --> 00:22:18,287
Uh, maybe she should try another Shiori bean, no, just to be sure.

366
00:22:18,947 --> 00:22:22,787
Come on, Moco-chan, don't tease Shiori.
Come on, Mococo, don't tease Shiori.

367
00:22:23,038 --> 00:22:27,598
The script doesn't say anything about a boss fight or Shiori wearing the cauldron.

368
00:22:29,208 --> 00:22:31,798
Shiori will remember this.

369
00:22:48,148 --> 00:22:49,888
All right, what do I do now?

370
00:22:51,138 --> 00:22:55,838
Then Yakuza say that you can use the cauldron to unlock the Blue Book of Responsibilities.

371
00:22:56,378 --> 00:23:01,798
All you need to do to complete that task is make us an apple pie.

372
00:23:02,168 --> 00:23:07,198
I'm sorry, you want me to make an apple pie with these?

373
00:23:08,388 --> 00:23:09,188
All right.

374
00:23:09,988 --> 00:23:11,588
Now what book is this?

375
00:23:12,548 --> 00:23:13,228
Oh.

376
00:23:23,788 --> 00:23:26,578
Hey, just wondering, but who wrote your script?

377
00:23:28,198 --> 00:23:31,848
Uh, I don't know, I guess it could have been anyone, really.

378
00:23:32,518 --> 00:23:34,938
Anyway, uh, where was I?

379
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:41,178
Oh, here, after the Yakuza's display of awesome magical abilities,

380
00:23:41,178 --> 00:23:47,378
the likes of which no other creatures could ever dream of attaining, Shiori took the greatest spoon ever crafted and used it to stir the apples.

381
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:53,638
The spoon, why is it so big?

382
00:23:55,158 --> 00:23:57,208
Hey, I could probably bonk you guys with this.

383
00:23:57,938 --> 00:23:59,358
Uh, no bonking, please.

384
00:23:59,638 --> 00:24:08,558
Oh, fine, I'll just use it for spoon things, just like that. All right, think this will actually make apple pie?

385
00:24:09,678 --> 00:24:11,008
Looks good.

386
00:24:13,368 --> 00:24:14,368
All right, let's see what's inside, then.

387
00:24:17,418 --> 00:24:18,038
Oh.

388
00:24:18,698 --> 00:24:21,088
Shiori takes the apple pie.

389
00:24:21,178 --> 00:24:29,928
Meanwhile, a friend, who may or may not be imaginary, but were definitely very hungry, look at the pie with anticipation.

390
00:24:33,308 --> 00:24:36,758
Can you do us a favor and leave the pie on the table so we can imagine eating it?

391
00:24:38,258 --> 00:24:42,578
Ah, my hungry puppies, I don't think you're allowed to eat apple pie, though.

392
00:24:42,578 --> 00:24:45,348
Please, please eat. I know it was really hard work.

393
00:24:45,348 --> 00:24:49,038
We'll see, we'll see.

394
00:25:05,145 --> 00:25:05,665
All right.

395
00:25:06,555 --> 00:25:08,615
Now that we have that apple pie,

396
00:25:09,155 --> 00:25:10,095
What now?

397
00:25:11,175 --> 00:25:13,475
Shiori put the pie on the table.

398
00:25:14,095 --> 00:25:17,695
Then she thought it would be nice to pour tofu milk for her friends too.

399
00:25:18,465 --> 00:25:19,765
I don't have tofu milk!

400
00:25:20,715 --> 00:25:21,095
Are you...

401
00:25:21,535 --> 00:25:22,995
Are you sure?

402
00:25:24,365 --> 00:25:26,745
I'm very sure that I don't have tofu milk.

403
00:25:27,835 --> 00:25:29,175
Uh, maybe we could just pretend?

404
00:25:32,455 --> 00:25:33,495
All right. That's a good idea.

405
00:25:35,365 --> 00:25:39,155
Gulp, gulp, gulp, gulp...

406
00:25:39,995 --> 00:25:42,555
It turns out imaginary milk is pretty good.

407
00:25:43,235 --> 00:25:46,635
Oh, give it here. I want it for my imaginary coffee.

408
00:25:47,495 --> 00:25:49,835
I'll trade you for a slice of the apple pie.

409
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:53,040
Deal! Shiori, can you give Mococo some pie?

410
00:25:53,975 --> 00:25:57,955
How am I going to give my imaginary friends my imaginary pie?

411
00:26:00,375 --> 00:26:01,795
But you know what? I think a better question would be...

412
00:26:02,875 --> 00:26:03,995
What do I do with this?

413
00:26:06,535 --> 00:26:10,635
Whoa! Cool! Wow!

414
00:26:11,275 --> 00:26:16,195
Oh, cool. Maybe you're supposed to wield it as your sword, like this?

415
00:26:16,335 --> 00:26:17,695
It does come with a plus-three to attack.

416
00:26:17,955 --> 00:26:19,935
Seriously, where are you seeing these numbers?

417
00:26:21,435 --> 00:26:23,815
Mococo-chan, why would a microphone be your weapon?

418
00:26:24,075 --> 00:26:28,495
Huh? I don't know, but if she's on an adventure, she's going to need a sword, okay?

419
00:26:29,175 --> 00:26:31,495
Yeah! But she's not an adventurer in the script.

420
00:26:34,975 --> 00:26:38,875
Well, maybe I want to add my own parts to this script. Is that really so wrong?

421
00:26:39,855 --> 00:26:42,555
Come on, she wants to go home. Don't worry, Shiori, I can help you with that.

422
00:26:43,835 --> 00:26:47,375
Why don't you go back to the bookshelf? At least one person's useful here.

423
00:26:48,915 --> 00:26:52,835
Don't worry, Shiori. This is almost over, I promise.

424
00:26:53,415 --> 00:26:55,815
But first, you need to unlock the Book of Memories.

425
00:26:56,375 --> 00:27:00,375
Do you remember ever getting lulled to sleep by a lullaby when you were a child?

426
00:27:00,715 --> 00:27:02,235
Of course not, I had no childhood.

427
00:27:02,615 --> 00:27:09,955
Well, to unlock the powers of the final book, you need to take the microphone and sing the yakuza to sleep. You got this, okay?

428
00:27:10,635 --> 00:27:12,475
All right, I'll do my best.

429
00:27:53,646 --> 00:27:56,326
いつもどう頑張って努力をしたところで
No matter how hard I try or how much effort I put in,

430
00:27:56,326 --> 00:27:58,686
指示示されるのは平均値
the results are always average.

431
00:27:59,646 --> 00:28:01,426
やってられないよ
I can't go on like this,

432
00:28:02,086 --> 00:28:04,946
くだらない評価に踊らされてばかり
constantly being manipulated by useless measures of worth.

433
00:28:05,166 --> 00:28:07,486
もう嫌になっちゃったこの人生
I've already come to hate this life,

434
00:28:08,126 --> 00:28:10,866
なら生まれ変わろうか
so, I think I'll restart my life.

435
00:28:11,306 --> 00:28:14,026
「異常」「異常」が胸を埋め尽くして
My chest is completely filled with "abnormality",

436
00:28:14,026 --> 00:28:16,186
普通じゃない自分になるの
I'm becoming a me that isn't normal.

437
00:28:16,526 --> 00:28:19,006
自問自答繰り返して手に入れたの
I ask myself over and over, "Did I get it?"

438
00:28:19,006 --> 00:28:21,126
新しいワタシを
A brand new me.

439
00:28:22,066 --> 00:28:23,306
ほら見てよ　ほら触れてよ
Look at me now, touch me right now,

440
00:28:23,586 --> 00:28:26,166
凡庸な服を捨て去って
I'll throw away my ordinary clothes.

441
00:28:26,526 --> 00:28:29,086
今サナギから　蝶になるの
Now, from my chrysalis, I'll become a butterfly.

442
00:28:29,086 --> 00:28:31,466
ありのまま全て見せつけて
I'll show off everything as it is.

443
00:28:31,466 --> 00:28:33,526
冷めきった舞台　演者はいない
There are no performers on this cooled-off stage,

444
00:28:33,526 --> 00:28:35,366
ならステップ刻んで one, two, three
so I'll beat out the steps, 1, 2, 3.

445
00:28:35,366 --> 00:28:37,466
踊らされるんじゃない　踊るのよ
I'm not being manipulated, I'm dancing!

446
00:28:37,806 --> 00:28:41,066
さぁ　さぁ　さぁ　狂って
Yeah, I'm going crazy!

447
00:28:57,186 --> 00:28:59,246
「普通」「普通」が呪いをかけてきて
"Normality" cast a curse on me,

448
00:28:59,466 --> 00:29:01,466
「異常」「異常」に憧れたの
and I yearned for "abnormality".

449
00:29:01,466 --> 00:29:04,186
異論、持論に興味などないからもう
I don't have any interest in your differing opinions,

450
00:29:04,186 --> 00:29:05,446
鍵をかけて
I've already locked the door.

451
00:29:06,206 --> 00:29:09,226
「好き」「嫌い」を疾うに通り越して
I went beyond "love" and "hate",

452
00:29:09,226 --> 00:29:11,826
「異常」に恋焦がれていたの
