What do you mean? I fall asleep to that song all the time.

485
00:31:07,745 --> 00:31:11,285
Oh, it looks like it worked, anyway.

486
00:31:11,643 --> 00:31:15,383
You got the last item! A nice... the beautiful purple heart.

487
00:31:16,323 --> 00:31:19,343
But what do I do with this now?

488
00:31:19,560 --> 00:31:24,080
I think the Myagusa are telling you to put the items in their slots on the table.

489
00:31:24,369 --> 00:31:27,809
Ah, I see. Alright, let's put this over here.

490
00:31:31,469 --> 00:31:34,069
And then we got the microphone here.

491
00:31:34,669 --> 00:31:42,109
And then last but not least, we got and here's my cauldron!

492
00:31:44,379 --> 00:31:47,399
Uh, wait, is something supposed to happen now?

493
00:31:47,499 --> 00:31:49,119
I think so. Mogu mogu?

494
00:31:49,379 --> 00:31:52,339
Huh? You didn't see it yet?

495
00:31:52,579 --> 00:31:57,819
No, all the books in your archive have been activated, and you can go home!

496
00:31:58,019 --> 00:32:01,359
Yes! Oh, oh, those books have unlocked the power of our friendship.

497
00:32:01,739 --> 00:32:06,959
With all of us working together, we'll be able to reopen the portal.

498
00:32:07,039 --> 00:32:09,159
We worked together? I think I did everything.

499
00:32:09,439 --> 00:32:14,699
And then Shiori approached the archway, eagerly awaiting the moment when...

500
00:32:14,699 --> 00:32:18,959
the combined strength of all of her friends would cause the portal to reactivate.

501
00:32:19,459 --> 00:32:22,579
Oh, so I can I can go home now, right?

502
00:32:22,919 --> 00:32:29,919
Uh, that that's weird. The power of friendship usually works.

503
00:32:30,379 --> 00:32:32,459
I know, right? Maybe those were all our social links?

504
00:32:32,539 --> 00:32:35,859
Maybe we're really not friends, huh? Maybe she needs to find an item to give her a plus three...
Maybe we're really not friends, huh? Maybe she needs to find an item...

505
00:32:36,799 --> 00:32:40,439
to give her a plus three to the power of friendship.

506
00:32:40,619 --> 00:32:43,699
But what item? I think I used everything.

507
00:32:44,299 --> 00:32:45,739
Mhm. Why not take the cue cards instead?

508
00:32:46,079 --> 00:32:48,139
Oh, let me look them over.

509
00:32:48,499 --> 00:32:53,379
I hope it helps. I don't want to be stuck here. Okay, uh, it it says here that...

510
00:32:54,319 --> 00:32:59,899
no matter how hard Shiori wanted to, she can't move backward.

511
00:33:00,719 --> 00:33:03,999
Uh, sorry, that wasn't very helpful after all.

512
00:33:04,279 --> 00:33:09,959
So what you're telling me is I'm going to be stuck in this Halloween-ish world, right? Yeah.

513
00:33:10,599 --> 00:33:15,979
Don't worry, Shiori, we're still here for you. Uh, maybe there's a silver lining in all of this.

514
00:33:16,199 --> 00:33:19,839
Okay, but I'm talking to a rock, two dogs, and one bird.

515
00:33:20,619 --> 00:33:25,159
Well, when you put it like that, maybe this isn't so great.

516
00:33:25,479 --> 00:33:29,879
But this is just the start of this world. I bet if you keep moving forward,

517
00:33:29,879 --> 00:33:34,299
you'll discover that it's not as scary a place as it looks now.

518
00:33:34,839 --> 00:33:39,159
Yeah, that's true. Plus, you've gained a whole new dimension.

519
00:33:39,339 --> 00:33:42,579
And, yeah, it's different, but it might be good, right?

520
00:33:43,139 --> 00:33:46,379
Yeah, I don't know. I mean, I look great.

521
00:33:47,039 --> 00:33:50,119
But I still like the old me.

522
00:33:51,179 --> 00:33:54,719
You're still the old you too, you know? You just got extra stuff now.

523
00:33:54,959 --> 00:33:56,599
On the next part of your journey.

524
00:33:56,599 --> 00:33:59,079
Yeah, exactly. Huh? Oh.

525
00:33:59,919 --> 00:34:03,999
Ah. But, you know, I wanted my character arc to be done.

526
00:34:04,279 --> 00:34:07,539
Sometimes I like having things stay the way they are.

527
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:12,679
Is that really all you want? Uh, well, duh.

528
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:19,059
But if all the pages in your books just are repeated over and over, you know, it gets pretty boring, right?

529
00:34:19,279 --> 00:34:22,579
And even if it didn't, moving forward is how we grow.

530
00:34:22,579 --> 00:34:24,539
Yeah. And how you find new games to play.

531
00:34:24,679 --> 00:34:26,099
Or new friends to make.
And new friends to make.

532
00:34:26,099 --> 00:34:32,459
And how we gained new friends. We would have never met in the first place had we not taken a chance on change.

533
00:34:33,299 --> 00:34:36,079
And your story would be boring without us, right?

534
00:34:36,359 --> 00:34:43,819
I guess. I mean, it's great having you guys as friends and have the novelites to keep me company.
I guess. I mean, it's great having you guys as friends and have the Novellites to keep me company.

535
00:34:44,299 --> 00:34:54,899
But, you know, sometimes I just want to look back, too. And if this is my book, then I should be able to decide what happens, right? I want to go at my own pace.

536
00:34:58,539 --> 00:34:59,899
More books?

537
00:35:01,133 --> 00:35:01,753
What's this?

538
00:35:03,083 --> 00:35:03,603
Oh.

539
00:35:07,183 --> 00:35:07,753
Oh, wow.

540
00:35:08,943 --> 00:35:10,583
Hang on, there's a cute item supposed to be...

541
00:35:11,953 --> 00:35:14,553
Well, hopefully this one's a good one.

542
00:35:15,063 --> 00:35:15,833
Oh.

543
00:35:15,883 --> 00:35:17,443
Okay, well, it says, "Don't worry, Shiori."

544
00:35:17,783 --> 00:35:21,813
"While your powers will continue to grow, and your journey will take you to realities as of yet unblessed to humanity..."

545
