602
00:41:15,864 --> 00:41:18,564
They're covered in water and stuff.

603
00:41:18,564 --> 00:41:21,064
Need to shake the droplets off.

604
00:41:21,564 --> 00:41:25,564
And you know what? My jacket makes me kind of feel gross too.

605
00:41:25,864 --> 00:41:28,064
I think it's time we take it off.

606
00:41:28,564 --> 00:41:31,064
Oh my, wow, what am I showing?

607
00:41:31,564 --> 00:41:33,564
Oh no, my arm, this arm, the other arm!

608
00:41:33,564 --> 00:41:36,064
Oh no, what am I doing?

609
00:41:36,564 --> 00:41:38,064
Oh, it feels a little bit better now.

610
00:41:38,064 --> 00:41:39,564
It's less wet, so, oh.

611
00:41:39,864 --> 00:41:42,564
This place is a lot prettier now.

612
00:41:42,864 --> 00:41:45,064
I can see the stars everywhere.

613
00:41:45,364 --> 00:41:48,564
It's a lot better than being in the other world with the voices in my head.

614
00:41:48,864 --> 00:41:53,064
When you hear nothing but "ooh" and "bow-wow" and "let's rock!"

615
00:41:53,264 --> 00:41:55,064
It gets a little tiring, to be honest.

616
00:41:55,364 --> 00:41:56,564
Ah, it's peaceful.

617
00:41:57,064 --> 00:41:59,064
You even see some beautiful flowers.

618
00:41:59,264 --> 00:42:00,564
They look like they're glowing.

619
00:42:01,064 --> 00:42:04,064
You should give congratulations to whoever the gardener is.

620
00:42:04,264 --> 00:42:06,064
